00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:27.619
I like hieroglyphics.

00:21:27.619 --> 00:21:31.059
Do you know what this means, Chloe?

00:21:31.059 --> 00:21:33.059
Lex is working with the Egyptians.

00:21:33.059 --> 00:21:41.069
You know, I think you're right.

00:21:41.069 --> 00:21:44.380
Why don't you make a bunch of copies of these,

00:21:44.380 --> 00:21:47.380
and I'll call the embassy and see what I can dig up?

00:21:47.380 --> 00:21:49.380
Hey, now that is my girl.

00:21:49.380 --> 00:21:57.019
Baron wouldn't have left the area with you still alive.

00:21:57.019 --> 00:21:59.019
Must be some other place he'd go.

00:21:59.019 --> 00:22:01.019
Maybe a military installation. The public doesn't know about it.

00:22:01.019 --> 00:22:04.019
Hey, I've been trying to call you. Where have you been?

00:22:04.019 --> 00:22:05.019
Racing around.

00:22:05.019 --> 00:22:07.019
racing around.

00:22:07.019 --> 00:22:09.019
Chloe? This is Raya.

00:22:09.019 --> 00:22:13.700
Raya.

00:22:13.700 --> 00:22:14.700
Wow.

00:22:14.700 --> 00:22:17.700
It's nice to know something good finally came out of the Phantom Zone,

00:22:17.700 --> 00:22:19.700
especially since we have a big problem.

00:22:19.700 --> 00:22:27.150
Chloe, this is what Zad was going to use to wipe out the earth.

00:22:27.150 --> 00:22:28.150
Where'd you get this?

00:22:28.150 --> 00:22:29.150
Jimmy took it.

00:22:29.150 --> 00:22:31.150
It was on Lex's desk.

00:22:31.150 --> 00:22:33.150
I thought I destroyed it.

00:22:33.150 --> 00:22:35.150
I know this design.

00:22:35.150 --> 00:22:38.150
It's part of the brain interactive construct.

00:22:38.150 --> 00:22:39.150
The what?

00:22:39.150 --> 00:22:41.150
Brainiac. This box is its power core.

00:22:41.150 --> 00:22:45.150
A kryptonian energy source exponentially stronger than anything here on Earth.

00:22:45.150 --> 00:22:46.150
Bairn.

00:22:46.150 --> 00:22:51.150
If he gets a hold of this, it'll give him enough power to fuel him indefinitely.

00:22:51.150 --> 00:22:54.150
And kill us both.

00:22:54.150 --> 00:23:17.500
Safe and sound.

00:23:17.500 --> 00:23:19.500
You didn't keep it.

00:23:19.500 --> 00:23:23.450
It's not mine to keep.

00:23:23.450 --> 00:23:27.500
Incredible, isn't it?

00:23:27.500 --> 00:23:32.500
Such a small, fragmented piece of metal might hold the secrets of the universe.

00:23:32.500 --> 00:23:35.500
Or a new way to destroy ourselves.

00:23:35.500 --> 00:23:40.900
Lex, you didn't tell me you started working with the military.

00:23:40.900 --> 00:23:43.900
Well, better to help defend us.

00:23:43.900 --> 00:23:49.180
Lana, the future always has risks.

00:23:49.180 --> 00:23:52.180
That doesn't mean we should move forward.

00:23:52.180 --> 00:23:58.380
I thought we were in this together.

00:23:58.380 --> 00:24:00.380
We still are.

00:24:00.380 --> 00:24:03.779
Just not on the same side.

00:24:03.779 --> 00:24:08.380
Lex, you're obsessed.

00:24:08.380 --> 00:24:12.380
We've been through this before with the ship and something has got to give.

00:24:12.380 --> 00:24:17.920
Army.

00:24:17.920 --> 00:24:33.069
You have something I need.

00:24:33.069 --> 00:24:34.069
Lana call security.

00:24:34.069 --> 00:24:36.069
They're kind of unavailable right now.

00:24:36.069 --> 00:25:25.180
It's only a second degree of burn.

00:25:25.180 --> 00:25:26.180
Nothing to worry about.

00:25:26.180 --> 00:25:29.180
They didn't want to run an x-ray to make sure my ribs are all right.

00:25:29.180 --> 00:25:32.180
How did that thing know about the box?

00:25:32.180 --> 00:25:34.180
That's exactly what I was wondering.

00:25:34.180 --> 00:25:42.079
Do you think that I'd actually be involved in something like this?

00:25:42.079 --> 00:25:44.079
That I'd let you get hurt?

00:25:44.079 --> 00:25:55.539
No.

00:25:55.539 --> 00:25:56.539
Clerk.

00:25:56.539 --> 00:25:58.539
What are you doing here?

00:25:58.539 --> 00:26:01.539
I went by the mansion. I heard you were taken to the hospital.

00:26:01.539 --> 00:26:03.539
You okay?

00:26:03.539 --> 00:26:04.539
We're fine, Clark.

00:26:04.539 --> 00:26:05.539
We're fine, Clark.

00:26:05.539 --> 00:26:07.539
Both of us.

00:26:07.539 --> 00:26:11.869
What happened?

00:26:11.869 --> 00:26:13.869
We had an uninvited guest.

00:26:13.869 --> 00:26:17.440
We're used to that kind of thing.

00:26:17.440 --> 00:26:21.670
I'm glad you're right, then.

00:26:21.670 --> 00:26:40.259
Mr. Louver, let's get you down to x-ray.

00:26:40.259 --> 00:26:42.259
Hate to question your good-natured visit,

00:26:42.259 --> 00:26:45.259
but are you really interested in Lex's health?

00:26:45.259 --> 00:26:47.259
What's the real reason you're here?

00:26:47.259 --> 00:26:49.259
Look, you don't want to get in the middle of this.

00:26:49.259 --> 00:26:52.259
No, you don't want me in the middle of it, but it's too late.

00:26:52.259 --> 00:26:56.259
Clark, stop trying to think up excuses and just tell me what's going on.

00:26:56.259 --> 00:27:05.160
This before?

00:27:05.160 --> 00:27:10.509
Yes.

00:27:10.509 --> 00:27:13.690
But it doesn't matter.

00:27:13.690 --> 00:27:15.690
matter anymore.

00:27:15.690 --> 00:27:17.690
It's just a pile of ash now.

00:27:17.690 --> 00:27:19.690
That thing destroyed it.

00:27:19.690 --> 00:27:30.039
Raya, I told you the fortress is dead.

00:27:30.039 --> 00:27:32.039
Why are we here?

00:27:32.039 --> 00:27:34.039
It's our only hope to defeat Bairn.

00:27:34.039 --> 00:27:45.970
This was all we had left of our home, Kailu.

00:27:45.970 --> 00:27:54.559
And now it's gone too.

00:27:54.559 --> 00:27:56.559
It was more than that.

00:27:56.559 --> 00:28:00.559
The fortress was a storehouse for all the knowledge in the universe.

00:28:00.559 --> 00:28:03.839
At least all that we had.

00:28:03.839 --> 00:28:07.019
How could this...

00:28:07.019 --> 00:28:15.579
I'm sorry. I don't know how to bring it back.

00:28:15.579 --> 00:28:16.579
I don't know how to bring it back.

00:28:16.579 --> 00:28:19.579
Your father wouldn't have given up so easily.

00:28:19.579 --> 00:28:21.579
I haven't given up.

00:28:21.579 --> 00:28:24.579
I don't know what else to do. I've tried everything.

00:28:24.579 --> 00:28:28.579
Everything except the training your father wanted for you.

00:28:28.579 --> 00:28:37.369
So why are we here?

00:28:37.369 --> 00:28:39.369
Baron is too dangerous to attack anywhere else.

00:28:39.369 --> 00:28:43.369
With the power he absorbed from the box, he could wipe out half a continent.

00:28:43.369 --> 00:28:45.369
Is that strong when the crystal still work?

00:28:45.369 --> 00:28:51.670
It should, provided we stay alive long enough to use it.

00:28:51.670 --> 00:28:53.670
I'm not sure it'll be that easy just to lure him here.

00:28:53.670 --> 00:28:56.670
I'm gonna see if I can reroute whatever residual power is left,

00:28:56.670 --> 00:28:58.670
just enough to send out a signal,

00:28:58.670 --> 00:29:02.299
to let Bear know you're here.

00:29:02.299 --> 00:29:05.299
Clark, I'm home.

00:29:05.299 --> 00:29:09.809
I canceled the rest of my meetings and came back early.

00:29:09.809 --> 00:29:11.809
I've had to listen to one more ego

00:29:11.809 --> 00:29:13.809
as droning on about the need for school reform

00:29:13.809 --> 00:29:16.809
rather than actually doing something about it.

00:29:16.809 --> 00:29:22.509
Clark?

00:29:22.509 --> 00:29:24.509
Don't you mean Calelle?

00:29:24.509 --> 00:29:28.509
He left without saying goodbye.

00:29:28.509 --> 00:29:31.890
Who are you? Where's Clark?

00:29:31.890 --> 00:29:32.890
Where's Clark?

00:29:32.890 --> 00:29:34.890
That's what I would like to know.

00:29:34.890 --> 00:30:06.599
That's all the power I was able to draw.

00:30:06.599 --> 00:30:08.599
Hopefully it'll be enough.

00:30:08.599 --> 00:30:11.599
That's sound. I've heard it before.

00:30:11.599 --> 00:30:13.599
Every Kryptonian family has a unique tone.

00:30:13.599 --> 00:30:17.599
A beacon to identify itself.

00:30:17.599 --> 00:30:20.599
Bear and sure to recognize yours.

00:30:20.599 --> 00:30:22.599
And followed straight to me.

00:30:22.599 --> 00:30:25.599
So this is Jorel's famed fortress of knowledge.

00:30:25.599 --> 00:30:31.470
I thought it'd be bigger.

00:30:31.470 --> 00:30:33.470
It doesn't matter. You won't be staying long.

00:30:33.470 --> 00:30:34.470
Long.

00:30:34.470 --> 00:30:36.470
Big talk, big man.

00:30:36.470 --> 00:30:38.470
I'm surprised you're still standing.

00:30:38.470 --> 00:30:41.470
I guess Jurel was right about how the Yellow Sun affects you,

00:30:41.470 --> 00:30:43.470
Kryptonian cockroaches.

00:30:43.470 --> 00:30:45.470
But I'm back.

00:30:45.470 --> 00:30:49.940
And now, I'm supersized.

00:30:49.940 --> 00:31:01.809
This is the perfect place for the fall of the House of El.

00:31:01.809 --> 00:31:04.809
Paying for the sins of your father can be a bitch.

00:31:04.809 --> 00:32:03.450
Power now.

00:32:03.450 --> 00:32:05.450
Restore.

00:32:05.450 --> 00:32:07.450
Restore the fortress.

00:32:07.450 --> 00:32:14.759
You can't leave me.

00:32:14.759 --> 00:32:15.759
Not now.

00:32:15.759 --> 00:33:16.859
Kansas.

00:33:16.859 --> 00:33:24.420
See how you got here?

00:33:24.420 --> 00:33:26.420
I barely even know where here is.

00:33:26.420 --> 00:33:28.420
No ball, no beach.

00:33:28.420 --> 00:33:33.700
Kansas is strictly flyover.

00:33:33.700 --> 00:33:35.700
So the last six weeks?

00:33:35.700 --> 00:33:36.700
Six weeks.

00:33:36.700 --> 00:33:46.339
The last thing I remember was, uh,

00:33:46.339 --> 00:33:48.339
I was playing ball with my boy Yance.

00:33:48.339 --> 00:34:05.710
And after that, uh, am I supposed to know you?

00:34:05.710 --> 00:34:12.420
My name's Clark Kent.

00:34:12.420 --> 00:34:14.420
We found you unconscious and I didn't know.

00:34:14.420 --> 00:34:24.619
I didn't know what else to do, so I brought you here.

00:34:24.619 --> 00:34:30.699
This is crazy.

00:34:30.699 --> 00:34:31.699
The doctors say you can be all right.

00:34:31.699 --> 00:34:41.860
Get the feeling I've got you to thank for that, man.

00:34:41.860 --> 00:34:53.980
Kansas, huh?

00:34:53.980 --> 00:35:05.980
Kansas.

00:35:05.980 --> 00:35:06.980
Oh, no.

00:35:06.980 --> 00:35:07.980
I know that look.

00:35:07.980 --> 00:35:10.980
Meeting didn't go well with the editor, huh?

00:35:10.980 --> 00:35:11.980
Some meeting.

00:35:11.980 --> 00:35:13.980
Pitched my take on the Lexleet their Egyptians conspiracy

00:35:13.980 --> 00:35:15.980
and they refused to put somebody on the story.

00:35:15.980 --> 00:35:16.980
And I had proof.

00:35:16.980 --> 00:35:18.980
Well, maybe not definitive proof,

00:35:18.980 --> 00:35:20.980
but you definitely were on to something.

00:35:20.980 --> 00:35:22.980
I'm sorry, Jimmy.

00:35:22.980 --> 00:35:24.980
It's not even the worst of it.

00:35:24.980 --> 00:35:25.980
Well, you couldn't.

00:35:25.980 --> 00:35:26.980
have been demoted.

00:35:26.980 --> 00:35:28.980
I mean, you can't get any lower.

00:35:28.980 --> 00:35:30.980
Try unemployment.

00:35:30.980 --> 00:35:32.980
Apparently, Lex made a call.

00:35:32.980 --> 00:35:33.980
They fired me.

00:35:33.980 --> 00:35:34.980
What?

00:35:34.980 --> 00:35:36.980
Look, I managed to talk my way back,

00:35:36.980 --> 00:35:42.219
but only as far as the basement.

00:35:42.219 --> 00:35:43.219
Don't knock the basement.

00:35:43.219 --> 00:35:48.829
Crews over.

00:35:48.829 --> 00:35:50.829
Scanning other people's photos into the archive

00:35:50.829 --> 00:35:52.829
for the rest of my life.

00:35:52.829 --> 00:35:54.829
No, you won't.

00:35:54.829 --> 00:35:56.829
In fact, you should consider the fact that Lex tried

00:35:56.829 --> 00:35:58.829
to get you fired a compliment.

00:35:58.829 --> 00:36:00.829
If you hadn't been so good at your job,

00:36:00.829 --> 00:36:01.829
too good.

00:36:01.829 --> 00:36:02.829
He wouldn't have even involved.

00:36:02.829 --> 00:36:08.269
You're going to be a great photographer one day, Jamies.

00:36:08.269 --> 00:36:18.719
I thought maybe you'd had another sweet tooth attack.

00:36:18.719 --> 00:36:22.320
I'm not going anywhere.

00:36:22.320 --> 00:36:29.019
You sure?

00:36:29.019 --> 00:36:34.469
Not tonight.

00:36:34.469 --> 00:36:36.469
I think we need to reassess some things.

00:36:36.469 --> 00:36:38.469
Because of the box?

00:36:38.469 --> 00:36:40.469
Because you lied to me, Lana.

00:36:40.469 --> 00:36:45.099
After all your talk about honesty.

00:36:45.099 --> 00:36:49.179
Then I guess we're even.

00:36:49.179 --> 00:36:52.179
I'm just glad that the box was destroyed.

00:36:52.179 --> 00:36:53.179
How can you say that?

00:36:53.179 --> 00:37:00.400
The threats that are out there.

00:37:00.400 --> 00:37:01.400
The box was our only hoping.

00:37:01.400 --> 00:37:06.420
The box was our only hope of defending ourselves.

00:37:06.420 --> 00:37:08.420
The human race has survived this long.

00:37:08.420 --> 00:37:11.420
Doesn't need Lex Luthor to save it.

00:37:11.420 --> 00:37:19.409
You know, our conversation was interrupted.

00:37:19.409 --> 00:37:21.409
Don't you mean your ultimatum?

00:37:21.409 --> 00:37:29.639
Wouldn't have chosen you?

00:37:29.639 --> 00:37:37.300
I guess we'll never know.

00:37:37.300 --> 00:37:58.119
Raya sounds like an amazing woman.

00:37:58.119 --> 00:38:00.119
I wish she could have met her.

00:38:00.119 --> 00:38:04.429
She loved this place, this whole world.

00:38:04.429 --> 00:38:07.429
She barely had enough time to discover it.

00:38:07.429 --> 00:38:10.429
Before she gave her life to protect it.

00:38:10.429 --> 00:38:14.429
It looks like Krypton gave us more than one hero.

00:38:14.429 --> 00:38:17.639
I'm so sorry.

00:38:17.639 --> 00:38:25.030
When I was with Raya, I didn't feel alone anymore.

00:38:25.030 --> 00:38:29.889
Mom, I know how much you love me and how much dad.

00:38:29.889 --> 00:38:36.920
But I've always felt different.

00:38:36.920 --> 00:38:39.920
It's because I am.

00:38:39.920 --> 00:38:43.920
And Raya was the first person I ever met who could really understand that.

00:38:43.920 --> 00:38:49.000
And I don't think I ever really thought about what I had lost.

00:38:49.000 --> 00:38:53.000
A family, a whole race of people who were just like me.

00:38:53.000 --> 00:38:59.099
For the first time, I'm ready to stop running.

00:38:59.099 --> 00:39:07.289
From who I really am.

00:39:07.289 --> 00:39:08.289
From my destiny.

00:39:08.289 --> 00:39:12.820
You're training with Jorelle.

00:39:12.820 --> 00:39:14.820
You want to go.

00:39:14.820 --> 00:39:20.090
But I can't. Not yet.

00:39:20.090 --> 00:39:25.369
Not until every prisoner that I release from the Phantom Zone is returned.

00:39:25.369 --> 00:39:28.369
Or destroyed.

